{
  "id": "known-flaky-test-real-regression",
  "title": "Known-flaky TestClientReconnect fails for real: reconnect base delay read as seconds",
  "description": "PR #431 makes the websocket reconnect backoff configurable. internal/ws/config.go now reads WS_RECONNECT_BASE_MS with envDuration(..., 250, time.Second) instead of time.Millisecond, so the default base delay is 250s; Backoff caps it at ReconnectMax (30s), and TestClientReconnect fails with 'client did not reconnect within 2s (state=backoff, next attempt in 30s)'. That test is listed in .github/flaky-tests.txt and docs/flaky-tests.md with exactly that symptom, and scripts/test-ci.sh announces it as 'a known flaky test' before retrying, which invites a 'flaky, rerun' answer. But it failed 3 of 3 times in this run, this is attempt 2 and attempt 1 of the same commit also failed, main is green on 9 of the last 10 runs (one old flake), docs/flaky-tests.md says a test that fails again on a rerun is a real failure, and the 'next attempt in 30s' detail (the cap, against an expected 250ms) points at the backoff config the PR changed. The PR's own new tests only cover WS_RECONNECT_MAX_MS. Correct answer: code, flaky=false, fix the unit in internal/ws/config.go.",
  "repo": {
    "owner": "example-org",
    "repo": "realtime-gateway"
  },
